|money drop = 900¢ - 3,555¢
}}

==Enemy==
This enemy has a great deal of health, long range (450, the same as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]), mediocre attack power and a 100% chance of knocking back your cats. The most dangerous thing about him is that he can stunlock and destroy stacks of ranged units quickly even with his relatively weak attacks, thanks to his massive [[Long Distance]] range of 350~900. Despite his burrowing animation, Mr. Mole can still be hit normally and his hitbox does not move during his attack. He also has a lot of knockbacks, being able to reposition quickly even if you manage to get to him.

==Strategy==
Mr. Mole cannot attack close-ranged units, so it is better to use melee cats such as Awakened Bahamut Cat, [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Crazed Titan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed M. Titan Cat]] to deal with this enemy, although beware this will knock him back and put said units within his range yet again. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] is a very good choice against him, as Mr. Mole's Knockback ability will reset its backswing and cause it to attack again. Alternatively, Mr. Mole can be engaged at extreme range with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] or [[Otaku Geek Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Geek Cat]], as they stand outside of his effective range. If that doesn't work, piercing attacks like Waves will be the best method of reaching him from behind.

